{"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Elements are tested in index order, 0 nearest the root. The table never holds two vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that test the same element with the same children, nor a vertex whose high child is the empty","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"family, so each family has one vertex: two ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/Family","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" values are equal exactly when they hold","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same sets. An element no set of a family contains never appears in its diagram, which keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the diagrams of sparse families small.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var diagram = ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram(elementCount: 3)","let f = diagram.family([[0, 1], [1, 2], [2]])","diagram.count(of: f)                                  \/\/ 3","let g = diagram.including(2, in: f)                   \/\/ {{1, 2}, {2}}","diagram.minimalSets(of: g) == diagram.family([[2]])   \/\/ true","diagram.join(diagram.single(0), g)                    \/\/ {{0, 1, 2}, {0, 2}}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Families are built by the mutating methods, which add vertices to the table and leave every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"existing family as it was; a family belongs to the table it was built in and its copies. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"table keeps every vertex it has made until "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/collectGarbage(keeping:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" drops the ones no kept"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"family reaches."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A shared table of zero-suppressed decision diagrams: families of sets drawn from the elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"0 ..< elementCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", each a directed acyclic graph whose vertices test one element and branch"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to a low child (the sets without it) and a high child (the sets with it, the element removed),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"down to the constants: the empty family and the family holding only the empty set (Minato,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“Zero-Suppressed BDDs for Set Manipulation in Combinatorial Problems”, 1993)."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/Family","doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/GraphView-swift.struct","doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/SetsView"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","title":"